--- TRACE LINE 34 ASSISTANT
The reference semantics models Python’s `round(float)` as a concrete-only operation, so I’m using an equivalent integer formulation of half-even rounding. For consecutive positive integers, the average is `(n + m) / 2`; on an odd sum, the exact `.5` tie rounds to whichever adjacent integer is even. This keeps the implementation fully symbolic in K.
--- TRACE LINE 35 custom_tool_call apply_patch
*** Begin Patch
*** Add File: /work/solution.py
+def rounded_avg(n, m):
+    if n > m:
+        return -1
+
+    total = n + m
+    average = total // 2
+    if total % 2 == 1:
+        if average % 2 == 1:
+            average = average + 1
+
+    return bin(average)
*** End Patch

