+sol = ast.parse(open('solution.py', encoding='utf-8').read()).body[0]
+test = ast.parse(open('runtime-tests.py', encoding='utf-8').read()).body[0]
+print('function_ast_equal=', ast.dump(sol, include_attributes=False) == ast.dump(test, include_attributes=False))
+PY
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+OUTPUT: function_ast_equal= True
+
+COMMAND: kompile verification.k --backend haskell --main-module ROUNDED-AVG-VERIFICATION --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX --output-definition audit-verification-kompiled
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT: Build succeeded. Only the supplied strLt unused-variable
+warnings were emitted.
+
+COMMAND: kprove spec.k --definition audit-verification-kompiled --spec-module ROUNDED-AVG-SPEC
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT: #Top
+
+COMMAND: kprove audit-claim-inverted.k --definition audit-verification-kompiled --spec-module AUDIT-CLAIM-INVERTED
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT: #Top
+
+COMMAND: kprove audit-claim-integral.k --definition audit-verification-kompiled --spec-module AUDIT-CLAIM-INTEGRAL
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT: #Top
+
+COMMAND: kprove audit-claim-half-down.k --definition audit-verification-kompiled --spec-module AUDIT-CLAIM-HALF-DOWN
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT: #Top
+
+COMMAND: kprove audit-claim-half-up.k --definition audit-verification-kompiled --spec-module AUDIT-CLAIM-HALF-UP
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT: #Top
+
+The four split files under /audit-output/evidence reproduce the four candidate
+claims verbatim in separate modules so each target was independently executed.

exec
